From: Dirk-Jan Faber <dfaber@victronenergy.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Remove prepack script

For building for Venus: npm prints the lifecycle script banner to stdout,
which npm-online-install takes as the name of the packed tarball. The
registry tarball already contains the built dist/, so prepack has nothing
to do here.
---
--- a/package.json
+++ b/package.json
@@ -44,8 +44,7 @@
     "test": "npm run lint && npm run test:unit",
     "test:unit": "jest",
     "test:watch": "jest --watch",
-    "lint": "eslint src/ test/",
-    "prepack": "node scripts/prepack.js"
+    "lint": "eslint src/ test/"
   },
   "keywords": [
     "node-red",
